WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
THE WAY THE WIND BLOWS

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.440
"YAMAKO GENERAL HOSPITAL"

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.820
They said you're malnourished?!

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.570
Are you not even capable of
feeding yourself?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.610
I've been busy taking care of Tsukasa,
that's all.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.200
In any case, hurry up and get changed!
A fall guy is coming to take your place.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.080
Hey! What the hell are you doing now?

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.080
The shoe polish was coming off
on my pillow.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.250
Shoe polish?!

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.340
When Tsukasa dyed his hair, changing
it back looked like a pain in the ass.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.350
So I tried mixing some shoe polish
into some soft wax instead.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.100
Quit fooling around!

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.690
I'm not. I did it carefully.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.360
You're here?

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.780
Yeah, the third floor. Bring him up
in the elevator.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.200
I'll be right back.
You'd better have changed.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.670
Damn Katsuragi must've left the door open.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:57.880
Huh?

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.680
I guess I'm still a bit lightheaded.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.390
No, that's not it.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.350
There's a breeze.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.900
I definitely feel a strange breeze.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.150
This is why I was against it!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.160
We should've finished him off
there and then!

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.290
What're you so flustered about?

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.210
We've made sure that nobody
can enter that room.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.710
And in any case, he's been crushed.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.300
Do you really think

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.470
a guy in that state could call for help

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.180
from Tsukasa's pet,
whom he's never even met?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.390
What I don't like

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.180
is that it's Tsukasa's pet
who got taken to hospital.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.270
Tsukasa might have suspected something

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.610
and deliberately got his pet...

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.570
Why would Tsukasa suspect anything?

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.490
Not even Katsuragi knows
that guy is alive.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.160
Even so, I'm worried.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:10.160
Jin is in Japan by herself,
and she's not only been working

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.830
with Satoru, but even
with Tsukasa's pet!

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:16.290
His pet is as all-powerful as Hayashi,

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.840
but only obeys orders from Tsukasa.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:23.130
It's like Tsukasa is walking around
with his own personal Doberman.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.340
It's too dangerous!

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.180
So tell me...

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:29.600
-What did Hayashi ever actually do?
-Huh?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.850
The all-powerful Hayashi, what was he
able to do exactly?

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.690
The only thing he ever managed

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.110
to do of his own accord

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.240
was to run away from the Company.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.700
So what is it about
Tsukasa's pet Doberman

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.830
that's got you so scared?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.580
Is it the bond between them?

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.960
Thanks to that kind of bond,
we were able to turn

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.040
the all-powerful Hayashi
into our lackey.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.710
The bonds between them

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.550
act as a chain fastened firmly
around their necks.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.810
It is their greatest weakness.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.270
And it is why we have kept that guy alive.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.980
Do you understand?

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:23.030
He is going to be the leash that enables
us to control Satoru and Tsukasa.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.080
This is weird...

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.790
Where's this wind coming from?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.500
I mean...

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.170
The AC is off... The windows are closed...

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.670
Hang on, my reflection...

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.430
My fringe isn't moving.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.260
Oh, I get it! This wind...

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.180
It's not real.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.690
It's the same sensation
I had with Tsukasa's water.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.770
An image...

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.980
It's somebody's image for sure!

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.440
Hey! I told you to get changed!

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.450
Katsuragi, I'm gonna step out for a bit.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.950
Like hell you are, you moron.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.410
You need to make this guy think
he's been hospitalized for malnourishment.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.210
It's you he's taking the fall for!

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.540
And that's not all.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:22.210
What about the doctors and nurses
who treated you?

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:25.340
Stop talking, Katsuragi.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.220
Just sit down and keep quiet,
or else you'll get in the way of my work.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.430
You were busy today, so you must be tired.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.480
Once this is done,
all you need to do is go to sleep.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.860
You did your job well, and this
is the final bit of clearing up.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.230
You can leave everything else to me
and get some rest.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.110
Okay... Katsuragi?

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.360
Y...Yeah.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.780
Time to say goodnight.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.250
Work can wait till later.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.670
I've got something to investigate first.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.250
There's gotta be an image user
somewhere in this hospital.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.260
I wonder what they're like?

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.050
I just need to follow
the sensation of the wind.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:19.310
Gotta be careful not to confuse it
with the real wind.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:24.270
No need to worry about it getting harder
to tell reality and images apart...

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.280
It's coming from several floors down.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.710
I've come all the way down
to the basement.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.050
Is someone really down here?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.550
But it's leading me this way.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.560
This is the place.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:00.810
Jeez, it's the mortuary...

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.730
But they're definitely in here.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.240
I caught Hayashi off guard
and entered his peak.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:20.540
Once you get into someone's peak,
it's easy to crush them.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.080
However, when Hayashi was crushed,
I got caught up in it as well.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.380
It seems I must have passed out.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.220
You're saying Katsuragi saw you passed out
and jumped to conclusions?

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.550
From what I heard, you looked like
you'd definitely been crushed.

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:41.100
If I'd been crushed, I couldn't be here
talking to you now, could I?

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:44.730
Anyway, you did well, Tsukasa.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.190
I have no qualms whatsoever
about making you my son.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:54.860
I've already taken care of
your adoption papers.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.700
Don't forget, I'm the elder brother.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.370
By the way, what did you do
with Hayashi's body?

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.620
Why does it matter?

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:07.830
Because I was unconscious, I wasn't able
to make sure he'd been completely crushed.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.420
I confirmed it. He was crushed.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.760
I even did a brain wave test.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.510
And the body?

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:20.430
What's up, Tsukasa? Do you wanna lay
some flowers on that traitor's grave?

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.430
There's no grave. We burned the body.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.480
That's a relief to hear.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:33.610
Considering the Satoru situation, it would
be a problem if there was a grave.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:38.160
We need Satoru to think
that Hayashi is still alive.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:41.700
To keep Satoru from thinking
anything is amiss,

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.410
I intend to introduce him to Meiling
as soon as possible.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.330
Since Meiling was shaped by Hayashi,

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:54.260
if Satoru meets her, he'll never suspect
that Hayashi's been killed by the Company.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:56.590
Indeed.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.720
We must be careful with Satoru.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:06.560
If he finds out you crushed Hayashi,
it'll cause a lot of problems.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:12.820
As a precaution, it'd be best for you
to have no further contact with him.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.320
This room is not in use.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.700
Damn, you scared me.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.080
Are you somebody's relative?
What's your name?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.450
Uh, no... I...

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.330
just wanna go into this room.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.960
It won't open. I told you it's not in use.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.250
Well, somebody's using it.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.970
Who are you? Are you not a relative?

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.430
If you're a patient,
you should be upstairs.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:41.220
You're a security guard, right?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:44.060
So you must have keys to
lots of rooms.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.970
Tick-tock...

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:52.520
I mustn't... give this key to anyone.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.700
If I open this door, an armed robber
is going to break into my house

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.990
and kill all my family as well.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.290
This guy's been hypnotized by someone.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.290
All right, listen up.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:12.710
If you don't open this door immediately,
a robber's gonna come.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.130
-Please, not a robber.
-It's okay.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:18.050
If you open this door, they won't come.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.180
So you'd better open it right now.
Then you'll be safe.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.220
Okay, I'll open it.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:24.850
I'll open it right now!

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:30.350
If he's been hypnotized, does that mean
someone from the Company did it?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.770
Okay, I opened it.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.460
What's with this guy?
Has he been crushed?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.050
No, there's still this wind image.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.470
That's proof he's not been fully crushed.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:09.470
It's the same as what happened to Tsukasa.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:13.350
By definition, our peaks are not genuine,

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:17.070
because they weren't made
from our own memories.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.860
From the very start, our peaks and valleys
haven't matched up.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.700
The power of our images

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.990
let us forcibly establish other people's
memories as our peaks and valleys.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.120
In times of crisis, it could be that
those same images

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.040
self-activate to buy us time
before we are fully crushed.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.460
Even so, why...?

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:40.710
Um...

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.930
We stopped the robber coming, right?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:45.890
Yeah.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:49.760
By the way, do you know who this guy is?

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.890
No idea. Who is he?

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.270
Okay. You can go now.

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:59.150
I'll let you know when I'm done.
Till then, don't let anyone in here.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:00.530
Got it.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.490
Looks like I'll have to ask
this guy in person...

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.370
So long as he's not been
completely crushed,

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.200
there should still be
a locus I can sync with.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.270
What the hell?

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.980
But, this is...

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.230
Get out...

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.530
of here.. now...

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.030
What?

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.030
Huh?

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.790
Tell me where...

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.920
I can find... Satoru...

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:03.420
Satoru? Do you know him?

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:05.590
Hey!

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.180
Hey! Wait!

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.220
Dammit. Come back!

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.350
We had a deal that Tsukasa wouldn't
be made to raise a pet.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.060
Why have you broken your promise?

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.310
The CEO didn't order anything.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.190
It was Tsukasa himself who asked
to be allowed a pet.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:26.440
He learned from the example of how
you found Satoru,

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:31.450
and searched hospitals throughout Asia
to find his own pet.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:34.700
He was probably lonely being
apart from you.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.710
-But now he's living happily with his pet.
-His pet?

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.210
That's just continuing the cycle!

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.380
This is how you people...

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:45.460
Hey!

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:47.840
It's too much...

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.720
I can't take any more...

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.470
You've shared your peak
plenty of times before.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.480
What's got you so twisted up
this time, Hayashi?

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.850
"Hayashi"? Did he say "Hayashi"?

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:05.020
This is how you make people
your slaves!

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.980
Haven't I done enough?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.650
So you don't care what happens
to Satoru, then?

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:13.870
Tsukasa hates you, you know.
He despises you.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:18.580
If Tsukasa teamed up with his pet,
they'd have no difficulty crushing Satoru.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.170
Tsukasa against Satoru? But why would...?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:23.420
Hey!

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:29.510
I don't...

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:33.590
I'm telling you to stay away
from Satoru, Tsukasa.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.010
-But...-What the hell...

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:38.060
What the hell
is this bald bastard saying?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.020
I will have to meet with Satoru.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.940
After all, it is me
who understands the most

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.980
about Meiling as well.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:48.530
If I can't meet Satoru,
how can I crush him?

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.360
Tsukasa.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:53.780
I'm saying this for your safety.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:58.200
You crushed Satoru's peak giver.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.660
If he finds that out through some
unfortunate turn of events,

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.670
it's you who will be in danger.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:08.800
There's no telling what Satoru might do

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.630
to the person who crushed Hayashi.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.050
Do you understand?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:19.140
Never mind Satoru, it's your pet
you need to do something about!

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:24.190
However much ability he has,
his lack of discipline is a problem.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.190
He's no use to us if he's constantly
mouthing off at Katsuragi.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.820
Hiroki...

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.200
will do what I tell him.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:37.370
Only doing what you tell him
isn't enough.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.000
What the Company needs

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.370
is a pet who will do
what the Company says.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:49.960
A pet who's only useful if you're there
with him isn't useful at all.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:54.090
You need to train him to be a pet
who'll follow orders

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:57.140
and work hard for the Company

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.510
even if you're not by his side.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.680
Now I get it! He's threatening me!

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:08.980
You shouldn't still be spending
all your time with your pet either.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:13.740
He's saying that if I don't obey him,
he's ready to set Satoru on me.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:17.320
He's saying he could reveal
to Satoru at any time

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:20.990
the fact that I crushed Mr. Hayashi.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:25.000
It's my fault... all of it...

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.880
Are you Mr. Hayashi, Satoru's peak giver?

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:32.090
No, wait! Don't disappear!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.470
Satoru's waiting for you!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:35.880
Satoru...

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.930
Satoru... Satoru...

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.390
I'm sorry, Satoru... It was a mistake...

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.310
My finding you...

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.100
was the start...

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:48.850
of everything...

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.360
Hey, wait! Stop!

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.150
Don't go! No!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.540
The locus... it vanished.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.090
No way. It can't have!

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.470
Shit! Where the hell did your image go?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.010
Don't you dare be crushed, dammit!

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.970
What the hell does all this mean?

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:31.020
What on earth's going on?

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.730
Why were they talking about Tsukasa?

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:35.990
So that's how it is!

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:39.700
He's demanding I hand Hiroki over
to the Company

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.990
if I want them to keep quiet
about Mr. Hayashi.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.540
Can you do that, Tsukasa?

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:51.250
What a dirty bastard!
Does he really think I'll give him Hiroki?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:52.960
Yes, of course.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.170
I expect I'll be busier from now on,

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:00.680
so I'd been thinking it was time to get
Hiroki to stand on his own two feet.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.220
Hiroki is my pet.

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:07.020
My pet whom I found and I raised!

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:10.520
He will only ever listen to me!

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:14.480
That's why our relationship is meaningful.
That's why...

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:17.780
I can trust Hiroki and only Hiroki!

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:20.200
Despite that,

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:23.950
this bastard intends to take
Hiroki away from me.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:29.040
He wants me to tell Hiroki
to do as the Company wishes.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.420
That's the same thing
Mr. Hayashi said to me!

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:36.800
Does he think I don't know
how that turned out!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.340
Incidentally,

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:41.180
I'd like to request a pistol
so I can protect myself.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.760
A pistol?

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.260
-As a precaution...-If this is how it is,

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.680
as soon as I get back to Japan,
I'll blow Satoru's brains out!

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:52.020
-in case Satoru finds out...-Everywhere I turn,

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.690
Satoru is there!

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.270
That bastard is always getting in my way!

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.690
that it was me who crushed Hayashi.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.070
I'd like to have...

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.280
something I could...

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:07.030
-protect myself with.-It's all Satoru's fault!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:09.540
All of it!

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.290
Get a hold of yourself, Tsukasa.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:17.800
How would you explain to your pet
why you were carrying a pistol around?

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:22.800
Yeah, only employees carry guns.
You're not Katsuragi, you know!

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.800
I'll let Hiroki... know... the situation.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:31.060
You're gonna voluntarily confess
to crushing Hayashi?

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.560
That's not a good idea.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:38.190
It would be dangerous for your pet
to know about Hayashi,

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:42.400
because that could lead to Satoru
finding out as well.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:48.080
It's not ideal for your pet to be doing
jobs with Satoru either.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:52.460
Let's not be overly worried here.
Satoru doesn't know anything yet.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.960
If you're concerned, we can provide you
with a bodyguard,

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.840
but you won't be getting a pistol.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.880
-That's it!
-One more thing.

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:05.090
You should probably move back
into a hotel,

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:07.720
especially since we'll be leaving
for Shanghai soon.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:10.260
There is still a way!

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:14.480
If Hiroki works with Satoru,
he'll be able to get close to him.

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:18.230
So Hiroki can crush Satoru.

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.730
Why were they talking about Tsukasa?

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:24.240
This guy is Satoru's peak giver, right?

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.990
I mean, I never heard...

00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:30.080
This is my first time
in a car with you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:30.990
"Hayashi"...?

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:34.040
But, he wasn't himself then.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:35.620
I mean...

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.880
Who are they calling a "pet" anyway?!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:41.630
C'mon, it's Tsukasa.

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:44.880
There's no way it could be true.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:47.890
I know Tsukasa better than anyone.

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:50.010
I can't let myself think about it.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:54.270
I don't have to think. It's obvious!
It looked exactly the same!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.020
The same as Tsukasa's peak
when he was crushed!

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:00.020
This guy is Tsukasa's peak giver.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:02.860
And yet, Tsukasa...

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:04.900
Tsukasa crushed him!

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:08.740
His own peak giver!
Why would you do that, Tsukasa?

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:14.620
How...?

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.790
How could anyone crush
their own peak giver?

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:55.050
Artist: Mai Machi
